{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Then the chiefs of Edom were dismayed, the mighty men of Moab.</b> When they saw these miracles, even though they knew that Israel would not come up against them for battle, nevertheless they were dismayed to witness it." "<b>Trembling takes hold of them.</b> May it be HaShem's will that trembling take hold of them and that they not rise up against us." "<b>All the inhabitants of Canaan melted away.</b> When the inhabitants of Canaan heard all this, they undoubtedly melted away, for they knew that Israel had come up against them to drive them out, as it says: וַנִּשְׁמַע וַיִּמַּס לְבָבֵנוּ וגו' (Joshua 2:11)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:41.119994645Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}